#  FinComp regulatory compliance assurance case - an OntoGSN TEMPLATE
#
#  Generated from : FinComp Assurance Case.drawio (draw.io, 4 pages)
#  Vocabulary     : serializations/ontogsn.ttl only - no augmentation, no alignment
#
#  Every element below is a placeholder. [Organization], <year>, <software>, <category>,
#  <ctrl_id>, <req_id>, <evid_id> and <issue_id> are the instantiation parameters; the
#  cardinality and multiplicity decorators on the relationships say how many times each
#  subtree is repeated when the template is instantiated. That is what makes this a
#  gsn:Template rather than an instantiated argument: "a template argument ... uses the core
#  GSN and argument pattern extension to construct an argument structure which requires no
#  further development", only instantiation.
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  How the diagram maps onto the ontology
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  DRAWN                                 WRITTEN AS
#  rectangle                             gsn:Goal
#  parallelogram                         gsn:Strategy
#  rounded rectangle                     gsn:Context
#  circle                                gsn:Solution
#  line, solid arrowhead                 gsn:supportedBy   + reified gsn:Relationship
#  line, hollow arrowhead                gsn:inContextOf   + reified gsn:Relationship
#  dashed line, open arrowhead           gsn:challenges    + reified gsn:Relationship
#  dotted line to a labelled triangle    gsn:attachedTo, from a gsn:InstantiationDataReference
#  small hollow triangle under a box     gsn:uninstantiated true
#  hollow ball on a line                 gsn:optional true
#  solid ball on a line                  gsn:multiple true, with the "1..N" text as
#                                        gsn:minCardinality / gsn:maxCardinality
#  page                                  gsn:Module + gsn:Argument, and a gsn:View
#  layer "Contents" / "Defeaters"        the module's risk / dialectic argument
#  goal box over a module box            an away goal: gsn:away true, gsn:public true
#
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Decisions the diagram does not make for you
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#  1. IDENTIFIERS. The three audit pages reuse the same local identifiers (G1, G1.1, C1, S1).
#     schema:identifier has to be unique - rules S25 and S41 invalidate both parties to a
#     clash - so each is qualified with its module: "JAP:G1.1.X". That is the convention the
#     diagram itself uses on the "Full" page, where the away goals read "JAP:G1". The three
#     elements drawn on that page keep their bare identifiers (G0, S0, C1).
#
#  2. AWAY GOALS. The "Full" page draws JAP:G1, BAIT:G1 and AML:G1 as away goals - a goal box
#     with a module box beneath it. An away goal repeats a claim declared elsewhere, so each is
#     ONE individual here: the top goal of the module named beneath it, marked gsn:away and
#     gsn:public. Rule S23 derives gsn:away from exactly this arrangement, so writing it out
#     agrees with what the rules would infer.
#
#  3. TEMPLATE ARGUMENTS. Each argument is typed both gsn:Argument and gsn:Template. The GSN
#     Community Standard calls the thing a "template argument", and OntoGSN keeps gsn:Pattern
#     apart from gsn:Argument without declaring them disjoint - rule S21 reifies a relationship
#     whose rdf:subject is a Template, which only makes sense if a template is an argument. The
#     Template side is what carries schema:description and gsn:intent; the Argument side is what
#     lets gsn:AssuranceCase and gsn:Module contain it, both of which admit only arguments.
#     None is published, so rules S21 and S22 leave them alone.
#
#  4. fc:M_Root IS NOT DRAWN as a module box. It stands for the "Full" page, so that the
#     support running from S0 into the three audit modules is a cross-module link the modular
#     extension can see.
#
#  5. TOP GOALS. gsn:top is computed, never chosen. A goal is top when no goal or strategy OF
#     ITS OWN MODULE supports it and it challenges nothing - the pinnacle claim of an argument,
#     not of the whole store - which is what rule S06 and gsnsh:TopGoalHasNoParentShape enforce.
#     That makes four: G0, and the top goal of each audit module. The three module top goals
#     keep their standing even though S0 reaches them, because S0 sits in another module; and
#     the challenge goals are excluded even though nothing supports them, because nothing
#     supports a defeater by construction.
#
#  6. STATEMENTS ARE TRANSCRIBED, NOT EDITED. Every gsn:statement is the text of its box as
#     drawn, including the diagram's own wording and its missing full stops; only draw.io's
#     markup and its soft hyphens have been removed. The statements on the modules and the
#     arguments, and every schema:description, gsn:intent and gsn:applicability, are the one
#     thing here that is authored rather than transcribed - the diagram has nowhere to put them.
#     fc:Arg_Root is a template on the strength of [Organization] alone: the "Full" page carries
#     that placeholder but no <parameters> and no decorators.
#
#  7. WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. gsn:valid, gsn:true, gsn:defeated and gsn:inDoubt are not
#     asserted: the diagram draws no defeated crosses and a template has nothing to be true of
#     yet. They are what rules S46 to S51 derive once the challenges are instantiated. Nothing
#     is typed gsn:Defeater either - that class is inferred by rule S52, never asserted. No
#     element is gsn:undeveloped: the diagram draws no undeveloped diamonds.

@prefix fc:     <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/example/fincomp#> .
@prefix gsn:    <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/ontology#> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/example/fincomp> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "FinComp regulatory compliance assurance case (template)"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """A GSN template assurance case for an organisation audited against IT General
Controls, BAIT and Anti-Money Laundering requirements, written with the OntoGSN ontology alone."""@en ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/OntoGSN/ontology> .


###############################################################################
#    The case
###############################################################################

fc:AC1 a gsn:AssuranceCase ;
    schema:identifier "AC1" ;
    rdfs:label "FinComp regulatory compliance assurance case (template)"@en ;
    gsn:statement "The [Organization]'s IT system is compliant with all regulatory requirements." ;
    gsn:contains fc:Arg_Root ,
                 fc:Arg_JAP ,
                 fc:Arg_JAP_Issues ,
                 fc:Arg_BAIT ,
                 fc:Arg_BAIT_Issues ,
                 fc:Arg_AML ,
                 fc:Arg_AML_Issues ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev1 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev2 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev3 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev4 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev5 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev6 ,
                 fc:JAP_Ev7 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Ev1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Ev2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Ev3 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Ev4 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Ev5 ,
                 fc:AML_Ev1 ,
                 fc:AML_Ev2 ,
                 fc:AML_Ev3 ,
                 fc:AML_Ev4 ,
                 fc:AML_Ev5 .


###############################################################################
#    Modules and template arguments
###############################################################################

#  One module per draw.io page. A module contains arguments, never elements directly:
#  gsn:Module restricts gsn:contains to arguments and modules, so a module's elements
#  are reached one hop further, through the argument. gsn:inModule - the one-hop form of
#  that traversal - is derived by rules S53 and S54 and is never authored.
#
#  Each page's two layers become two arguments of the same module, because
#  gsn:argumentType admits one value: the "Contents" layer is the risk argument and the
#  "Defeaters" layer the dialectic one. Keeping both in one module matters - were they
#  separate modules, rule S23 would mark every element supported across the layer
#  boundary as an away element, which is not what the diagram draws.

fc:M_Root a gsn:Module ;
    schema:identifier "M-Root" ;
    rdfs:label "Regulatory compliance module"@en ;
    gsn:statement "The module that ties the three end-of-year audit modules together into the overall regulatory compliance claim." ;
    gsn:contract false ;
    gsn:contains fc:Arg_Root .

fc:Arg_Root a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-Root" ;
    rdfs:label "Regulatory compliance argument"@en ;
    schema:description "The top-level argument of the case: compliance with all regulatory requirements is argued over the end-of-year audits, one module per regulation. The audit modules are reached as away goals."@en ;
    gsn:intent "Establish that an organisation’s IT system is compliant with every regulation it is audited against, by decomposing over the audits."@en ;
    gsn:applicability "Applies to an organisation each of whose regulatory obligations is discharged by a recurring external audit, one module per regulation."@en ;
    gsn:statement "Argument over all end-of-year audits." ;
    gsn:argumentType "risk" ;
    gsn:structured true ;
    gsn:published false ;
    gsn:final false ;
    gsn:contains fc:Root_G0 ,
                 fc:Root_C1 ,
                 fc:Root_S0 .


fc:M_JAP a gsn:Module ;
    schema:identifier "M-JAP" ;
    rdfs:label "Module JAP"@en ;
    gsn:statement "The IT General Controls argument, evidenced by the end-of-year audits (Jahresabschlussprüfung)." ;
    gsn:contract false ;
    gsn:contains fc:Arg_JAP , fc:Arg_JAP_Issues .

fc:Arg_JAP a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-JAP" ;
    rdfs:label "JAP audit argument"@en ;
    schema:description "Argues IT General Controls compliance from the end-of-year audits: one claim per audited year, then per audited software, then per ITGC category and control, evidenced by the auditor’s control files. A second branch carries the controls that apply to the IT system as a whole rather than to a single piece of software."@en ;
    gsn:intent "Establish ITGC compliance for an organisation from the evidence its end-of-year audits produce, without fixing the number of years, systems or controls in advance."@en ;
    gsn:applicability "Applies where the auditor issues a per-year control catalogue covering the IT General Controls, broken down by audited software, and where some of those controls apply to the IT system as a whole rather than to one system."@en ;
    gsn:statement "Argument from end-of-year auditing (JAP)." ;
    gsn:argumentType "risk" ;
    gsn:structured true ;
    gsn:published false ;
    gsn:final false ;
    gsn:contains fc:JAP_G1 ,
                 fc:JAP_C1 ,
                 fc:JAP_S1 ,
                 fc:JAP_C2 ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1 ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1 ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X ,
                 fc:JAP_S1_1_X_1 ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X_Y ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X_1_N_M ,
                 fc:JAP_S1_1_X_Y ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X_Y_Z ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_1_N ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_1_N_M ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y_Z ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X_Y_W ,
                 fc:JAP_Sn1_1_X_1_N_M ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y_W ,
                 fc:JAP_Sn1_1_X_Y_W .

fc:Arg_JAP_Issues a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-JAP-Issues" ;
    rdfs:label "JAP issues argument"@en ;
    schema:description "The dialectic half of the JAP template: for every control claim and every control file, a challenge stands ready to be instantiated from the auditor’s comments, and a remediation branch claims each raised issue has been addressed."@en ;
    gsn:intent "Record the auditor’s objections as challenges rather than leaving them outside the argument, and claim their resolution where it has been shown."@en ;
    gsn:applicability "Applies where the auditor records objections against named controls or named evidence files, and where the organisation tracks each objection through to a resolution it can evidence."@en ;
    gsn:statement "The issues auditors have raised against the JAP argument, and the claims that each has since been addressed." ;
    gsn:argumentType "dialectic" ;
    gsn:structured true ;
    gsn:published false ;
    gsn:final false ;
    gsn:contains fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y2 ,
                 fc:JAP_C1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:JAP_Sn1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_1_N_M_I ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_1_N_M_D ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y_W_I ,
                 fc:JAP_Sn1_1_X_1_N_M_D ,
                 fc:JAP_G1_1_X_Y_W_D ,
                 fc:JAP_Sn1_1_X_Y_W_D .


fc:M_BAIT a gsn:Module ;
    schema:identifier "M-BAIT" ;
    rdfs:label "Module BAIT"@en ;
    gsn:statement "The Bankaufsichtliche Anforderungen an die IT argument, evidenced by the end-of-year BAIT audits." ;
    gsn:contract false ;
    gsn:contains fc:Arg_BAIT , fc:Arg_BAIT_Issues .

fc:Arg_BAIT a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-BAIT" ;
    rdfs:label "BAIT audit argument"@en ;
    schema:description "Argues BAIT compliance from the end-of-year audits: one claim per audited year, then one per BAIT requirement, evidenced by the auditor’s requirement files."@en ;
    gsn:intent "Establish BAIT compliance for an organisation from the evidence its end-of-year audits produce, without fixing the number of years or requirements in advance."@en ;
    gsn:applicability "Applies where the auditor issues a per-year requirement catalogue for the BAIT requirements, with one file of evidence per requirement."@en ;
    gsn:statement "Argument from end-of-year BAIT auditing." ;
    gsn:argumentType "risk" ;
    gsn:structured true ;
    gsn:published false ;
    gsn:final false ;
    gsn:contains fc:BAIT_G1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_C1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_S1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_C2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_C1_1 ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1_X ,
                 fc:BAIT_C1_1_X ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1_X_Y ,
                 fc:BAIT_C1_1_X_Y ,
                 fc:BAIT_Sn1_1_X_Y .

fc:Arg_BAIT_Issues a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-BAIT-Issues" ;
    rdfs:label "BAIT issues argument"@en ;
    schema:description "The dialectic half of the BAIT template: a challenge per requirement claim and per requirement file, and a remediation branch claiming each raised issue has been addressed."@en ;
    gsn:intent "Record the auditor’s objections as challenges rather than leaving them outside the argument, and claim their resolution where it has been shown."@en ;
    gsn:applicability "Applies where the auditor records objections against named controls or named evidence files, and where the organisation tracks each objection through to a resolution it can evidence."@en ;
    gsn:statement "The issues auditors have raised against the BAIT argument, and the claims that each has since been addressed." ;
    gsn:argumentType "dialectic" ;
    gsn:structured true ;
    gsn:published false ;
    gsn:final false ;
    gsn:contains fc:BAIT_G1_1_X_Y2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1_X_Y_I ,
                 fc:BAIT_C1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_G1_1_X_Y_D ,
                 fc:BAIT_Sn1_1_X_Y2_Z2 ,
                 fc:BAIT_Sn1_1_X_Y_D .


fc:M_AML a gsn:Module ;
    schema:identifier "M-AML" ;
    rdfs:label "Module AML"@en ;
    gsn:statement "The Anti-Money Laundering argument, evidenced by the end-of-year AML audits." ;
    gsn:contract false ;
    gsn:contains fc:Arg_AML , fc:Arg_AML_Issues .

fc:Arg_AML a gsn:Argument , gsn:Template ;
    schema:identifier "Arg-AML" ;
